# 17-CXP / post purchase experience

**Goes here.** Order confirmation to second order, and everything a customer feels
along the way. Journey mapping, packaging and inserts, shipping communication,
returns process, review requests and timing, loyalty and VIP, recovery playbooks,
customer delight, retention and repeat rate levers.

## Not here

- The proposition that got them to buy -> 03-OFF
- A one-off personal gesture to a handful of top customers -> 19-WLD
- The mechanics of sending emails and SMS -> 14-EML
- Staffing the support desk and SLAs -> 21-OPS
- Review acquisition inside Amazon policy -> 22-AMZ

**The CXP and WLD line is cost per order.** A handwritten note in every order has a
cost per order and a measurable effect on repeat rate, so it is CXP. A personal letter
to your 50 highest-value customers is unmeasurable and one-off, so it is WLD.

**The CXP and OPS line.** CXP is the content of the customer interaction. OPS is the
desk that handles it.

**The CXP and EML line.** CXP decides what a customer should hear and when. EML is the
flow logic, deliverability and sending.

