## Topics

journey mapping, packaging and inserts, shipping communication, returns process,
review requests and timing, loyalty and VIP, recovery playbooks, customer delight,
repeat rate levers.

## Look for

Cost per order for each tactic. Effect on repeat rate where stated. Timing of every
message. Tier thresholds. Recovery policies with cost caps.

## Skip

Delight ideas with no cost attached, because delight without a cost is a wish.
Introductory "what is customer experience" essays and annual trend pieces, which a
good model already knows. General CX thought leadership with no ecommerce mechanism.

## The timing insight

Ask for the review when the job is done, not a fixed number of days after delivery.
Time to value is recoverable from review text and support ticket timing. A review
asked at the right moment names the objection other buyers carry, and becomes a proof
asset for 07-LPG.

## Scope mix

Baseline: accurate shipping and delivery messages, a findable return policy, a working
review request, and a recovery path that exists.

## Done when

Every tactic in the library has a cost per order and an expected effect on repeat
rate.

